#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""herdr-hibernate — auto-hibernate idle coding-agent tabs in Herdr.

Kills the agent process tree of idle panes (freeing 500 MB-2 GB each) and
replaces it with a tiny bash stub that resumes the exact session on Enter.
Supports Claude Code, Codex, and Grok; only agents with a proven on-disk
resume path are ever touched. Panes and tabs are never closed. Dry-run by
default.

Hibernation survives reboots: each hibernated pane gets a stub script under
~/.config/herdr-hibernate/panes/. A .bashrc hook re-arms that stub the moment
Herdr spawns a fresh shell in the pane, and `restore` re-arms any pane whose
stub died (Herdr restart, machine reboot, stub killed).

Nothing is retained for a closed tab: when a pane disappears its record and
stub script are deleted outright (after a short grace window), and the log is
size-capped. The tool only ever holds data for panes that currently exist.

Subcommands: watch | scan | restore | hibernate <pane_id>
              hibernate-workspace <workspace_id> | wake-workspace <workspace_id>
              workspace-toggle [workspace_id] | forget <pane_id>
              status | install | uninstall
"""

